  m_Name: DinuguanReflection
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dishName: Adobo
  dishSprite: {fileID: 0}
  pages:
  - Well done. You have just prepared one of the oldest Filipino dishes still cooked
    today.
  - The vinegar you added did two jobs at once.
  - It stabilised the blood against clotting, and it carried the dish forward through
    time,
  - "allowing families without refrigerators to feast on today\u2019s pig for days
    afterwards."
  - When you serve dinuguan with puto, you are serving the sweet alongside the deep,
    the new alongside the old,
  - 'the quiet with the bold. This is how Filipino families have thought about meals
    for centuries. '
